# mini-SWE's native runtime inside the task sandbox, for agent sessions. The agent server's own environment
# (pyproject.toml) keeps the SWE-Gym fork that /run uses. LiteLLM's Responses adapter imports MCP v2 types even
# for ordinary function tools, so this runtime carries MCP v2; the task-local MCP CLI uses the same runtime.
# requirements.txt locks the full closure: after changing this file, regenerate it with the command in its header.
